            <ArticleTitle>[Coenaesthesia after infection with Varicella zoster virus. The psychodynamic meaning of suffering a children's disease at adult age].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>688-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case report is presented of a 33-year-old male who developed coenaesthesia after suffering from chickenpox. While central nervous involvement of the herpes zoster virus infection was not found, suffering a children's disease at an adult age proved an important psychodynamic factor for release of the coenaesthetic symptomatology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
